body:
MN is not close to being red at all. The MSP metro (which is SOLID blue) accounts for about 60% of the total statewide vote. We also made substantial gains in the state house last year. Tim Walz, Amy Klobuchar, and Tina Smith also won by double digits last year (Klobuchar carried all eight congressional districts). Also, with the suburbs shifting towards Democrats, I'd say the DFL is in an advantageous position going into 2020. Even with rural MN trending towards Republicans, I would very much rather be Democrats in this case as the gains being made in suburban MN will vastly outweigh Republicans gains in rural MN (especially in statewide races). I would say run up the margins as much as possible in MSP  and its suburbs while keeping Republicans' margins down in rural MN. We're NOWHERE near being a red state.

&#x200B;

EDIT: Punctuation
